>kavuri@lips3.ecn.purdue.edu (Surya N Kavuri ) writes:

>  (Q1) I have seen a whole array of monsters but the 
>       most difficult was a titan which I faced in level 15.
>       (I am at level 26 now).  This guy blew away my
>       blessed +6 cloak of protection (GRR...).  I was 
>       close to dying but my fire horn saved me.  Do
>       I need a particular intrinsic to kill this guy ?

    Magic resistance. If you don't have it I would suggest you simply avoid
all magic using creatures (Lichs, Golden Nagas and Titans). If you *insist*
on killing titans use a powerful wand - cold, fire, lightning or death or use
poisoned arrows. Using a cockatrice corpse is not recommended since the titan 
or other creature can destroy your gloves. Unfortunately, lichs are resistant
to cold, fire and poison, they also are immune to a wand of death so if you 
don't have a wand of lightning avoid them if possible. If you have to fight a
lich at least make sure you have cold resistance. Also fight them in a corridor
if possible since they can summon monsters. Having a ring of conflict can make
things a lot easier.
       

>  (Q2) I had the intrinsic "see invisible" quite early in the
>       game.  At level 21, I was blinded by lightning from 
>       a Dragon.  I lost my intrinsic after that! 
>       I had to seek out another floating eye to get it back.
>       What is so "intrinsic" about it if I can loose it ?

    I think you mean telepathy here. Generally, one loses telepathy by killing
a friendly human (shopkeeper, temple priest etc.). The only other way to lose 
intrinsics is by gremlins.


